        "nombre": "BATALLÓN DE INFANTERÍA MOTORIZADO N° 37",
        "resena": "It was created by Resolución Suprema of February 4, 1941, in the context of the conflict with Ecuador. The unit was initially organized as Batallón de Infantería N° 37. In September 1949, it received the historic name “Pucará,” in honor of the victories of the Ejército de la Resistencia during the Campaña de La Breña. On April 1, 1969, it was reorganized and adopted the designation Batallón de Infantería Motorizado “Pucará” N° 37. From February 1983 onward, it participated in the counter-subversive struggle, occupying bases in Olmos, Tocto, and Abra Porculla. On January 26, 1995, it deployed to Tumbes to join the Peruvian defensive deployment during the Alto Cenepa conflict. Its headquarters is located at cuartel El Tablazo, district of Huanchaco, province of Trujillo."
