        "resena": "LA AMAZONÍA “ SARGENTO 1° DEMETRIO ACOSTA CHUEZ N° 85 The Batallón de Infantería de Selva de Protección de la Amazonía N° 85 has maintained a presence in Ampama since before 1991. It was organized to protect the northeastern border through land, riverine, and airmobile operations in the río Santiago basin. During the 1995 Conflicto del Cenepa, it defended the Cahuide, Chiqueiza, and Pachacútec surveillance posts and other sectors near the Cordillera del Cóndor. Its patrols engaged in combat in the río Santiago sector, carrying out reconnaissance, position-defense, and national-sovereignty protection missions. Its headquarters is at the Ampama garrison, district of Río Santiago, province of Condorcanqui, Amazonas region."
