        "nombre": "GRUPO DE ARTILLERÍA DE CAMPAÑA N° 111",
        "resena": "LA MAR” N° 111 It was created by Decreto Supremo on September 6, 1937, under the original designation Grupo de Artillería Nº 6. On September 19, 1949, it received the honorary name “Mariscal La Mar,” and since March 11, 1969, it has borne the number 111. In July 1941, it moved from cuartel Santa Catalina in Lima to Tumbes to take part in the conflict with Ecuador. After the campaign, it remained in Tumbes until March 1942 and was subsequently transferred to cuartel Grau in Piura. During the 1981 conflicto de la Cordillera del Cóndor, it occupied positions opposite Papayal, prepared to support operations with its fires. Its headquarters is in Piura la Vieja, district of La Matanza, province of Morropón."
