        "nombre": "GRUPO DE ARTILLERÍA DE CAMPAÑA “ CAP JUAN",
        "resena": "It was created by Resolución Suprema N° 47-73/FU of December 3, 1973. On December 6 of that year, it was named after Captain Juan Antonio Portugal, a hero of the Campaña de la Breña.\n\nIt was initially established at the Escuela de Artillería and, in April 1974, was transferred to the facilities of RC N° 1.\n\nIt later occupied the Cuartel “Mariscal Cáceres” at Fuerte Rímac and, from 1981, the Cuartel “José Gálvez.”\n\nDuring the 1981 border conflict, it remained ready to support operations in the Teatro de Operaciones del Norte. In January 1995, it deployed north to support the military operations conducted during the conflict of the Cenepa.\n\nIts headquarters is located at Fuerte Papayal, district of Papayal, province of Zarumilla, region of Tumbes."
