      "en": {
        "nombre": "BATALLÓN DE INFANTERÍA MOTORIZADO “ ´PUCARÁ”",
        "resena": "N° 37\n\nIt was created by Resolución Suprema of February 4, 1941, in the context of the conflict with Ecuador. The unit was initially organized as Batallón de Infantería N° 37.\n\nIn September 1949, it received the historic name “Pucará,” in honor of the victories of the Ejército de la Resistencia during the Campaña de La Breña.\n\nOn April 1, 1969, it was reorganized and adopted the designation Batallón de Infantería Motorizado “Pucará” N° 37. From February 1983 onward, it participated in the counter-subversive struggle, occupying bases in Olmos, Tocto, and Abra Porculla.\n\nOn January 26, 1995, it deployed to Tumbes to join the Peruvian defensive deployment during the Alto Cenepa conflict.\n\nIts headquarters is located at cuartel El Tablazo, district of Huanchaco, province of Trujillo."
      },
