      "en": {
        "nombre": "REGIMIENTO DE CABALLERÍA BLINDADO “LANCEROS DE",
        "resena": "The Regimiento de Caballería Blindado N° 5 (RCB N° 5) was created by Decreto Supremo on December 28, 1846.\n\nIt originated from the Regimiento «Guías» N° 2, named «Lanceros de Torata» in memory of the battle fought on January 19, 1823.\n\nDuring the Guerra del Pacífico, its predecessor units fought in the battles of San Juan and Miraflores in January 1881.\n\nIt reappeared in 1895 as «Lanceros de Torata» N° 1 and, the following year, was redesignated «Carabineros de Torata» N° 5.\n\nDuring the 1941 Peruvian–Ecuadorian conflict, it played a prominent role in the batalla de Zarumilla and in operations conducted in Ecuadorian territory.\n\nIts current headquarters is in Poechos, district of Lancones, province of Sullana, Piura region; it was formerly stationed in Querecotillo."
      },
