        "resena": "It was created by RS Nº 24-CIE of August 7, 1941, initially as an organic element of the 1ª División Ligera.\n\nIn September 1942, it was stationed in Suyo, provincia fronteriza de Ayabaca, and subsequently began a series of movements throughout the national territory.\n\nDuring its history, it was stationed in Chocope, Ilo, Tarata, and Huacho, adapting its organization to the Ejército’s operational requirements. In 1993, it joined the then 1.ª División de Fuerzas Especiales as a reinforcement unit.\n\nIn February 1995, it participated in the conflicto del Cenepa through joint patrols with Batallón de Comandos N.º 19, taking part in operations in the sector Tiwinza.\n\nIts headquarters are in the ciudad de Andahuaylas, región Apurímac."
