        "resena": "By Resolución Suprema Nº 341 IGE/IM of September 19, 1949, it received the name «General San Martín».\n\nIts historical background includes deployment to Callejón de Huaylas in 1916 and to the Cajamarca provinces of Chota and Cutervo in 1923.\n\nIn 1927, it completed a memorable horseback march from Lima to Arequipa and then continued to Santa Lucía, Puno, where it remained until 1933. During the Campaña Militar de 1941, it was transferred to the northern border and joined the reserve of Agrupamiento Norte, commanded by general Eloy G. Ureta.\n\nIn 1995, it sent two combat platoons—81 mm mortars and air defense—to support operations during the conflicto del Cenepa.\n\nIt is stationed at cuartel Coronel Gregorio Albarracín in ciudad de Tacna."
