      "en": {
        "nombre": "REGIMIENTO DE CABALLERÍA BLINDADO “MARISCAL",
        "resena": "It was created by Decreto Supremo Nº 268-IGE of October 24, 1942, under the initial designation Grupo de Reconocimiento.\n\nIn 1945, it became Regimiento de Reconocimiento Mecanizado and, in 1949, received the honorary name «Mariscal Castilla».\n\nFollowing successive reorganizations, Orden General N.º 5 de la División Blindada of February 24, 1962, established its current designation.\n\nDuring its early years, it occupied cuartel «José Gálvez» in Rímac, where it was equipped with AMX-13 light tanks.\n\nIt participated in important national activities, including the so-called «Operación Ayacucho» of 1964.\n\nIn June 1974, it was transferred to Tacna and, beginning in October 1975, was stationed at cuartel «Tarapacá».\n\nIt currently retains its designation and headquarters in Tacna."
