        "resena": "It was created by Decreto Supremo of January 26, 1963, and began operations on February 1 of that year.\n\nIt was organized in Cusco on the basis of two companies from Lima and Puerto Maldonado, under the command of teniente coronel Alcibíades Sáenz Barsallo.\n\nIts first missions included constructing the Ollantaytambo–Umasbamba and Amparaes Colca roads to integrate the valleys of Cusco.\n\nIt later participated in constructing the Puerto Bermúdez and San Luis de Shuaro Satipo roads, the latter inaugurated in December 1973.\n\nOn December 17, 1989, its personnel fought an MRTA terrorist base in Chaparral, where sargento Zenón Turco Herrera died heroically.\n\nIts headquarters are in La Merced, provincia de Chanchamayo, Junín."
