        "resena": "N° 47\n\nIt was created on November 17, 1943, by Resolución Suprema Nº 4/EMGE, and was initially organized in the city of Iquitos.\n\nIn September 1949, it received the name “Alfonso Ugarte”, in tribute to the Peruvian hero of the batallas de Tarapacá y Arica.\n\nBeginning in 1955, it assumed surveillance of the Morona-Pastaza sector, protecting an extensive area of the northeastern border.\n\nIt participated in the operaciones de la Cordillera del Cóndor of 1981 and the Conflicto del Cenepa of 1995.\n\nIts headquarters are in guarnición de Sargento Puño, distrito de Morona, provincia de Datem del Marañón, región Loreto."
