        "resena": "Its origins date back to 1916, when Compañía de Zapadores Trocheros Nº 5 was organized to open roads in Alto Marañón and northeastern Peru.\n\nOn September 19, 1951, it was created as Batallón de Ingeniería Nº 5 and officially activated on January 1, 1952.\n\nIt later received the name of mariscal Óscar R. Benavides, hero of the combate de La Pedrera and former President of the Republic.\n\nThroughout its history, it has built highways, roads, camps, and basic services, while also supporting pacification operations in the Amazonian region.\n\nIts headquarters are at campamento militar “Alfredo Vargas Guerra”, in the city of Iquitos, región Loreto."
