        "resena": "The Compañía de Ingeniería de Servicios Nº 115 was initially created as Batallón de Ingeniería de Servicios Nº 115 on January 1, 1981. It originated as an organic unit of the 5ª División de Servicios of the former Quinta Región Militar and initially occupied cuartel “Ramón Castilla”. In January 1981, it participated in the conflicto de la Cordillera del Cóndor, supplying and maintaining engineering materials and equipment used by combat units. In 1988, during the reorganization of logistics organizations, the battalion was reduced and transformed into the current Compañía de Ingeniería de Servicios Nº 115. In 2003, it received personnel and resources from the deactivated Batallón de Asuntos Civiles Nº 115. Its headquarters are at Fuerte Militar “Soldado Alfredo Vargas Guerra”, distrito de Iquitos, provincia de Maynas, Loreto."
