        "resena": "A fire-support Major Unit subordinate to the I División de Ejército. It was created by Decreto Supremo Nº 106 on January 1, 1975, during the government of Division General Juan Velasco Alvarado. On May 1, 1976, its Command and Staff were organized to plan, coordinate, and direct the operations of its subordinate artillery groups. During the 1995 Conflicto del Alto Cenepa, it provided fire support to the Ejército de Operaciones del Norte and received units from other garrisons. Its name honors Colonel José Joaquín Inclán Gonzales Vigil, commander of the Peruvian 7ª División during the defense of Arica. Its headquarters is at Cuartel «Grau», avenida San Martín, Piura."
