        "resena": "Its origins date back to 1916, when Compañía de Zapadores N.º 5 was created in Puno and later renamed Compañía de Ingenieros Nº 4. It was constituted as Batallón de Ingeniería Nº 4 by Decreto Supremo of December 2, 1925. In 1949, it received the name of teniente coronel Pedro La Rosa, a patriot who joined the Ejército Libertador organized by San Martín in Huaura. La Rosa served in the Legión Peruana de la Guardia, fought at Torata and Moquegua, and died heroically in Iquique on February 14, 1823. In 1968, it adopted the designation Batallón de Ingeniería de Combate Motorizado “Tte Crl La Rosa” Nº 4, which it retains to this day. Throughout its history, it has participated in the construction, rehabilitation, and maintenance of roads and other works in Puno, Cusco, and Arequipa. It is stationed in ciudad de Juliaca, provincia de San Román, región Puno."
