        "nombre": "BATALLÓN DE INGENIERÍA DE CONSTRUCCIÓN “LA BREÑA” N° 2",
        "resena": "Its origins lie in the reorganization of engineering units tasked with infrastructure construction and support for national development. It adopted the name Batallón de Ingeniería y Construcción Nº 2 and received the historic name “La Breña”, in tribute to the Campaña de la Resistencia. Throughout its history, it has built and rehabilitated highways, bridges, local roads, and other works in difficult-to-access areas. Its work acquired special importance in the central jungle, helping integrate rural communities and strengthen the State's presence. It has also supported security and pacification operations conducted within the valle de los ríos Apurímac, Ene y Mantaro. Its headquarters are in provincia de Satipo, departamento de Junín."
