        "resena": "Its origins date back to mid-1920, when Destacamento Mixto de Montaña was organized to protect eastern Peru. In 1921, it became part of Regimiento “Cazadores de Oriente” Nº 17 and was later constituted as Batallón Mixto Nº 17. During the conflicto con Colombia of 1932–1933, it formed part of Agrupamiento Leticia, responsible for defending the Amazonian territories. On September 19, 1949, it received the historic name “Tarapacá”, in tribute to the victory achieved during the Guerra del Pacífico. It is currently an organic unit of the V División de Ejército, responsible for territorial surveillance and protection of the Amazonía. Its headquarters are in Pijuayal, distrito de Pebas, provincia de Mariscal Ramón Castilla, región Loreto."
